70	83	no-promise-executor-return	returnsValue	This returns a value from a promise executor, and nothing can ever read it. The Promise constructor ignores whatever the executor returns, so a value here is either dead code or, more often, a missing `resolve` call the author believed was implicit. The usual cause is `return fetch(...)` where `resolve(fetch(...))` was meant, which leaves the promise pending forever.	0	0
